While I agree with most of Patric said, I believe the issue involves
more than a defunct DevTeam.

The problem, as I see it, is that there is nobody who is (a) willing
to take over and (b) unify the community behind him (or her).

True, on one hand we have the DevTeam being, excuse my vernacular,
dicks by not releasing bugfixes (or even the bug reports) for more
than 7 years; but on the other hand we have *two* variants in active
development, neither of which claims to be the next incarnation (well,
it could be worse, they could both be fighting over the title).

So as long as there two variants which are quite similar and neither
clearly superior, the community will remain fractured and none of the
variants will gain the necessary traction.

Let's say I find a bug in Vanilla.  Do I spend time to reproduce and
document it?  Who shall I send the report to?  The DevTeam, and have
it disappear into Gehennom for another 7 years?  To the Spork or to
the Un devs?  What if it no longer there, or is there but cannot be
reproduced in the same way because it's hidden by code changes?  Or do
I just say to hell with it?

Patric mentioned Crawl.  To which I can reply by saying that it worked
largely due to the fact that Stone Soup was the only viable variant.

I understand that Derek wants to to take his project in the direction
he likes most and that Patric wants to do the same.  I can't fault
them for that, but unless this situation changes, there will be no
more "official" NH.

And to those that ask what if somebody tries to take leadership and
then the DevTeam comes out of the woods bearing version 4.0 which
proves to be the best thing since sliced bread, is beautifully coded
and and runs on anything from digital watches to space shuttles?

Firstly, I don't put that much faith in the DevTeam and secondly, even
if that happened, $LEADER would be justified in saying "thank you for
the sources, we will take them and integrate whatever we feel like
into the $NEW_OFFICIAL_NH because we don't want you stalling
development for another decade".  I, for one, would support $LEADER
wholeheartedly and I believe that the rest of the community will do
the same because most of them are sick and tired of the situation.

Unfortunately, neither Derek nor Patric showed any inclination to work
toward that goal so my guess is that there will never be any new
"official" version and the community will remain split among similar-
but-somewhat-different versions with some preferring Spork, others
preferring Un and yet others sticking with Vanilla and hoping the
DevTeam's second coming.


